{"type":"standard","title":"Carol and Eric Hafner","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Carol and Eric Hafner</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q131322406","titles":{"canonical":"Carol_and_Eric_Hafner","normalized":"Carol and Eric Hafner","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Carol and Eric Hafner</span></span>"},"pageid":78288779,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1371530771","tid":"59511e17-a1b0-11f1-9620-108860a49432","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:43:41Z","description":"American political activists","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Carol_and_Eric_Hafner"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carol_and_Eric_Hafner?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Carol_and_Eric_Hafner"}},"extract":"\nCarol Hafner and her son, Eric G. Hafner, are American political activists and perennial candidates, a mother and son known for running in United States House of Representatives elections in states of which they are not residents or have never visited. This is allowed by Article One of the United States Constitution which only requires that representatives live in the state in which they are chosen when elected.","extract_html":"<p>\n<b>Carol Hafner</b> and her son, <b>Eric G. Hafner</b>, are American political activists and perennial candidates, a mother and son known for running in United States House of Representatives elections in states of which they are not residents or have never visited. This is allowed by Article One of the United States Constitution which only requires that representatives live in the state in which they are chosen <i>when elected</i>.</p>"}